#!/bin/sh
chown -R www-data:www-data /var/lib/tachyon
chown -R root:root /usr/share/tachyon/

# Replaces: tachyon (<< 4.4.3~) lets this package take over the files the old
# "tachyon" package owned, so the install no longer stops on a conflict (#154).
# It does not remove that package though, and what stays behind is a whole older
# copy of the application under the same directory, its own index.php, include.php
# and setup.php included. Several releases up to 4.4.3 closed real security holes,
# so leaving it there is not a tidiness question.
if dpkg-query -W -f='${Status}' tachyon 2>/dev/null | grep -q 'install ok installed'; then
	cat <<'WARN' >&2

The old "tachyon" package is still installed. It holds an older copy of
Tachyon under /usr/share/tachyon, which may still be reachable by the web
server and is missing the security fixes in 4.4.0 through 4.4.3. Remove it:

    apt remove tachyon

(Debian's unrelated "tachyon" ray tracer uses /usr/bin/tachyon. If that is the
one you have, you can ignore this.)

WARN
fi
